Z||000000||LoW_KeY||12-23-2001||12:33 PM||||Well.. I remember reading on the fiero-list mailing group that people used ford injectors I think? they said they were the best ones that they've used.<P>But what should I use for injectors, cam and lifters? I plan on porting, balancing and getting 10.1 pistons.<P>I'm mostly just worried about the injectors I know some people said they've grabbed some and it didn't help and others said they grabbed the ford ones and it was a huge difference, any feed back would be much appreciated, thanks.<P>-KC<BR><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/low_keysig.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ironhedno3||12-23-2001||10:59 PM||||ive got some brand new 19lb 3800 buick injectors if your interested..these are brand new out of a gm replacement engine||||reg||6
Z||000002||Cooter||12-23-2001||11:32 PM||||Not so much Ford injectors, but new injectors. The Ford Motorsports disk type 24 pound injectors that I have are made by Bosche. The 19 pound that I put in a friend's car were Ford Motorsports, but pintle type with no identifying markings anywhere. From what you are telling us about your engine, 19 pound injectors will be plenty. ||||reg||1
